===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The or an act of taking.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Report to Congress: Impacts of California Sea Lions and Pacific Harbor Seals on Salmonids and West Coast Ecosystems|publisher=U.S. Department of Commerce, National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration, National Marine Fisheries Service|year=1999|page=32|pageurl=https://books.google.ca/books?id=_RwXAQAAIAAJ&pg=PA32|passage=The 1994 Amendments address the incidental '''take''' of marine mammals in the course of commercial fishing, not the direct lethal '''take''' of pinnipeds for management purposes.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Lissa Evans|title=Their Finest Hour and a Half|location=London{{nb...}}|publisher=[[w:Doubleday (publisher)|Doubleday]]|year=2009|page=321|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/theirfinesthoura0000evan/page/321/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-385-61423-8|passage='I saw you in Norfolk doing twenty-odd '''takes''' with that fisherman chap and it looked perfect in the rushes.'}}
# Something that is taken; a [[haul]].
## Money that is taken in, (legal or illegal) proceeds, income; {{lb|en|in particular}} profits.
##* {{RQ:NYT|author=w:Paul Krugman|title=The Depravity of Climate-Change Denial|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230517193607/https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/26/opinion/climate-change-denial-republican.html|date=26 November 2018|passage=Why would anyone go along with such things? Money is still the main answer: Almost all prominent climate deniers are on the fossil-fuel '''take'''.}}
##: {{ux|en|He wants half of the '''take''' if he helps with the job.}}
##: {{ux|en|The mayor is on the '''take'''.}}
## The or a quantity of [[fish]], [[game]] animals or [[pelt]]s, etc which have been taken at one time; [[catch]].
# An [[interpretation]] or [[view]], [[opinion]] or [[assessment]]; [[perspective]]; a [[statement]] expressing such a [[position]].
#: {{ux|en|What's your '''take''' on this issue, Fred?}}
#: {{ux|en|Another unsolicited maths '''take''': talking about quotients in terms of "equivalence classes" or cosets is really unnatural.}}
#* {{RQ:Wired|author=w:Jenna Wortham|title=So Long, and Thanks for All the Tips!|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230606063403/https://www.wired.com/2008/11/so-long-and-tha-2/|date=19 November 2008|passage=Should you crave a fix of my '''take''' on tech culture, get the urge to build a 3-D home cinema or want the skivvy on the latest internet memes or robo-romances, you can keep a close eye on me via Twitter or drop me a line at my new digs.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=w:Ben Mathis-Lilley|title=Fox News Military Analyst Says John McCain Broke Under Torture and Gave Secrets to North Vietnamese|work=[[w:Slate (magazine)|Slate]]|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221128221827/https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2018/05/fox-news-analyst-john-mccain-broke-under-torture.html|date=10 May 2018|passage=I wrote Thursday morning that the Washington Post had printed a column that qualified as the worst '''take''' on the debate over whether Gina Haspel, who supported the torture of "War on Terror" detainees, should become CIA director. I was very wrong. ''This'' is the worst '''take''':}}
#* {{RQ:New Yorker|author=Sheldon Pearce|title=Kendrick Lamar and the Mantle of Black Genius|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230804095354/https://www.newyorker.com/culture/cultural-comment/kendrick-lamar-and-the-mantle-of-black-genius|date=26 October 2020|passage=Another of the victims, Michael Brown, was an aspiring rapper himself and a Lamar fan. Though Kendrick's controversial '''take''' on Brown's death is somewhat glossed over, the book is constantly putting into context how the rapper's art is a product of the same trauma and working in service to the Black communities that experienced that trauma.}}
#* {{RQ:WaPo|author=Sarah Lyon|title=In a small space, do you really need a dining table?|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/home/2022/09/14/small-spaces-dining-table/|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/Ebv74|archivedate=15 September 2022|date=14 September 2022|passage=We turned to the experts to get their '''takes''' on whether you truly need a dining table in a small home. For some designers, having one is nonnegotiable; others have found ways around it. Read on to see what works best for you.}}
# An [[approach]], a (distinct) [[treatment]].
#: {{ux|en|a new '''take''' on a traditional dish}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Tim Richardson|title=Great Gardens of America|location=London|publisher=w:Frances Lincoln Limited|year=2009|page=87|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/greatgardensofam0000rich/page/87/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-711-22886-3|passage=Whatever the provenance, the result is a delightfully novel '''take''' on a stalwart, often deadening Victorian feature.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:David Walliams|title=Camp David: The Autobiography|location=London|publisher=w:Penguin Books|year=2012|year_published=2013|page=288|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/campdavidautobio0000wall/page/288/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-241-95772-1|passage=''The League of Gentlemen'' was all set in one town; ''The Fast Show'' did what it said on the tin, the sketches came thick and fast; ''Goodness Gracious Me'' was a brilliant '''take''' on British Asian culture.}}
#* {{RQ:Rolling Stone|author=Brittany Spanos|title=Celine Dion Delivers Powerful Queen Cover at Billboard Music Awards|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230326114241/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/celine-dion-delivers-powerful-queen-cover-at-billboard-music-awards-55927/|date=23 May 2016|passage=As part of her acceptance speech for the Billboard Icon Award during the show, Dion showed off her well-honed Las Vegas showmanship during her '''take''' on the Queen classic and statement of endurance.}}
# {{lb|en|film}} A [[scene]] [[record]]ed ([[film]]ed) at one time, without an [[interruption]] or [[break]]; a recording of such a scene.
#: {{ux|en|It's a '''take'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Act seven, scene three, '''take''' two.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} A recording of a musical performance made during an uninterrupted single recording period.
# A visible ([[facial]]) [[response]] to something, especially something [[unexpected]]; a facial gesture in response to an event.
#: {{ux|en|did a [[double take]] and then a triple '''take'''}}
#: {{ux|en|I did a '''take''' when I saw the new car in the driveway.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:William Shatner|author2=[[w:Ron Goulart|&#91;Ron Goulart&#93;]]|title=TekLords|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:G. P. Putnam's Sons|year=1991|page=48|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/teklords0000shat/page/48/mode/1up|isbn=0-399-13616-9|passage="When our client mentioned Dr. Chesterton, you did a '''take''' that was perceptible to one with my trained eye. Know the gent, ''amigo''?"}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Laura McBride|title=Catch a Falling Starr: A Novel|location=New York, N.Y.{{nb...}}|publisher=w:iUniverse, Inc.|year=2007|page=138|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/catchfallingstar0000mcbr/page/138/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-595-44510-3|passage=Biddy did a {{'}}'''take'''{{'}} and stared at Mandy speechless for a moment—then she fled back to the kitchen.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Carsten Stroud|title=The Homecoming|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Alfred A. Knopf|year=2013|page=301|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/homecoming0000stro_s7o3/page/301/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-307-70096-4|passage=He's a stone-cold snake, Nick, but he's our stone—cold snake. Keep tugging on hanging threads and one day your pants will fall off." ¶ Nick did a '''take''', grinning in spite of his miserable mood. "How, exactly, would that work?" ¶ Mavis shrugged, grinned right back at him.}}
# {{lb|en|medicine}} An instance of [[successful]] [[inoculation]]/[[vaccination]].
# {{lb|en|rugby|cricket}} A [[catch]] of the ball (in cricket, especially one by the [[wicket-keeper]]).
# {{lb|en|printing}} The quantity of [[copy]] given to a [[compositor]] at one time.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:John Southward|chapter=XXI|title=Practical Printing: A Handbook of the Art of Typography|edition=second|location=London|publisher=J. M. Powell & Son|year=1884|page=197|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/practicalprinti00powegoog/page/197/mode/1up|passage=When the copy arrives, it is taken in hand by the printer, who first of all divides it into "'''takes'''" or short portions, distributing these among the various compositors. A '''take''' usually consists of a little more than a stickful of matter, but it varies sometimes, for if a new paragraph occurs it is not overlooked. These '''takes''' are carefully numbered, and a list is kept of the compositors who take the several pieces.}}

