Page 6 Template talk:is-conj: -------- begin text --------
{{ping|Numberguy6|Fenakhay|Mårtensås}} I'd like to propose rearranging this template into a more compact form to match Old Norse ({{tl|non-conj-table}}) and other Germanic verb tables of a similar type (e.g. [[wäggunge#Conjugation|Saterland Frisian]] and [[obrenna#Conjugation|Bavarian]]). Significantly, the compact look would improve the experience of the ~50% of Wiktionary readers who access the site from mobiles.

As far as the active and mediopassive voices are concerned, the template could be just about copied over from {{tl|non-conj-table}}, with changes to add the supine and fused imperative forms. 

I'd also like to offer a second proposal, which is to move the declension table from the verb entry to the past participle entry. I am not aware of other highly-inflected languages which include the declension of the past participle on the ''verb'' lemma entry (if there are, please point me to them!). This practice leads to an excessively long set of inflected forms in a single entry.

Any thoughts on these two proposals? [[User:This, that and the other|This, that and the other]] ([[User talk:This, that and the other|talk]]) 06:24, 20 March 2025 (UTC)
-------- end text --------
