Page 10 put the cart before the horse: -------- begin text --------
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-put the cart before the horse.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|put<,,put> the cart before the horse}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To put things in the [[wrong]] [[order]] or with the wrong [[priorities]]; to put something [[inconsequential]] as more important than something more [[essential]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1898|author=w:Julian Hawthorne|title=The History of the United States|chapter=1
|passage=The hour had struck; and with it, as always, appeared the man. So it has ever been in the history of the world; though we, with characteristic vanity, uniformly '''put the cart before the horse''', and declare that it is the man that brings the hour.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2 Dec 1957|title=Corruption of the Mind|titleurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20071121080237/http://www.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,825322,00.html|journal=Time
|passage=To attempt to remove the armaments before removing these substantive conflicts of interest is to '''put the cart before the horse'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=08 Dec 79|volume=7|number=20|journal=Gay Community News|page=11|author=Dick Bowring|title=HATS Helps Gay Alcoholics|quotee=Elizabeth Hjeltness|text=Saying, as some people do, "If I could get these other problems straightened out, then the drinking would take care of itself" is '''putting the cart before the horse'''. You can't deal with emotions like love and hate and rage when you're numbing yourself with chemicals.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=27 Jul 2005|author=David D. Kirkpatrick|title=Timing of Hearings and Vote Stalls Confirmation Talks|titleurl=http://www.nytimes.com/2005/07/27/politics/politicsspecial1/27confirm.html|journal=New York Times|accessdate=6 Nov. 2008
|passage=Mr. Schumer said that the idea of agreeing to a date for a vote before the committee had held hearings was "'''to put the cart before horse'''."}}

