Page 11 font: -------- begin text --------
{{also|fönt|főnt}}
==English==
[[File:Colonna - la Maddalena acquasantiera 1050336.JPG|thumb|holy water '''font''']]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/fɒnt/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/fɑnt/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-font.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒnt|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|en|fountain-related}}
From {{inh|en|ang|font}}, an early borrowing from {{der|en|la|fons|fōns, fontis|fountain}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|receptacle for holy water}} {{lb|en|Christianity}} A [[receptacle]] in a church for [[holy water]], especially one used in [[baptism]].
#: {{syn|en|stoup<id:receptacle for holy water>}}
#: {{hypo|en|baptismal font}}
#: {{ux|en|She dipped her fingers in the '''font''' and [[cross oneself|crossed herself]].}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Hymns for the Amusement of Children|chapter=[[s:en:Hymns for the Amusement of Children (1791)/Moderation|Moderation]]|year=1791|author=w:Christopher Smart|passage=Blessed be God, that, at the '''font''', /⁠ My sponsors bound me to the call / Of Christ in England to confront / The world, the flesh, the fiend and all.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Catholic Encyclopedia|volume=2|chapter=[[s:en:Catholic Encyclopedia (1913)/Baptismal Font|Baptismal Font]]|author=w:John Bertram Peterson|year=1913|passage=In the Apostolic Age, as in Jewish times (John, iii, 23), baptism was administered without special '''fonts''', at the seaside or in streams or pools of water (Acts, viii, 38); {{...}}}}
# {{senseid|en|receptacle for lamp oil}} A [[receptacle]] for [[lamp oil]] in a [[lamp]].

