===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|en|melting-and-foundry-related}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|fonte}}, feminine past participle of verb {{m|fro|fondre||to melt}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|fount}} {{qualifier|UK}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|subset of a typeface or its forms}} {{lb|en|typography}} A set of [[glyph]]s of unified design, belonging to one [[typeface]] (e.g., Helvetica), [[style]] (e.g., [[italic]]), and [[weight]] (e.g., [[bold]]). Usually representing the [[letter]]s of an [[alphabet]] and its supplementary [[character]]s.
## In metal [[typesetting]], a set of type [[sort]]s in one size.
## In [[phototypesetting]], a set of [[pattern]]s forming glyphs of any size, or the [[film]] they are stored on.
## In [[digital]] typesetting, a set of glyphs in a single style, representing one or more alphabets or [[writing system]]s, or the computer code representing it.
# {{senseid|en|typeface, broadly}} {{lb|en|originally computing|typography|informal}} A [[typeface]].
# {{senseid|en|computer file encoding a typeface or subset thereof}} {{lb|en|computing|typography|metonymically}} A computer [[file]] containing the [[code]] used to draw and compose the glyphs of one or more typographic fonts on a computer [[display]] or [[printer]].
#: {{ux|en|They bought a license for the Gulliver '''font''' and installed that '''font''' on several machines.}}

