* {{alt|en|anglicize|Anglicize||North American|and|Oxford British spelling}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|anglicus|alt=anglic(us)}} {{suf|en||ise}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæŋɡlɪsaɪz/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-anglicize.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}} {{qualifier|non-Oxford British spelling}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make [[English]], as to customs, culture, pronunciation, spelling, or style.
#: {{hyper|en|q1=of [[word]]s|naturalize<id:linguistics>|paronymize}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:W. H. Auden|year=1970|title=A Certain World|page=267|location=New York|isbn=0670209945|publisher=Viking Press|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/certainworldcomm00aude/page/267/mode/1up|passage=Someone who is translating into English a German novel, the hero of which is named Heinrich, will leave the name as it is; he will not '''Anglicize''' it into Henry.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2022/dec/09/what-does-the-lensa-ai-app-do-with-my-selfies-self-portrait-photos-magic-avatar-generator-gone-viral|title=What does the Lensa AI app do with my self portraits and why has it gone viral?|date=2022-12-08|work=The Guardian|author=Caitlin Cassidy|passage=Other users of non-anglo descent have also alleged Lensa whitened their skin and '''anglicised''' their features, a common complaint of image-editing software on platforms like TikTok.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To dub or translate into English.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become English.

