Page 26 Anglesey: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Possibly of {{der|en|non|-}} origin, from {{m|non|Ǫngullsey|t=hook island}} ({{m|non|ǫngull}} + {{m|non|ey}}) or {{m|non|Ǫnglisey|t=Ǫngli's island}}, the name {{m|non|Ǫngli}} itself being a variant of {{m|non|Ǫngull}} and from the former noun. Folk etymology confused the name with that of the [[Angles]]. More at [[w:Anglesey#Name|Anglesey]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæŋ.ɡəl.siː/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Anglesey.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyphenation|en|An|gle|sey}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-prop}}

# {{place|en|An <<island>> and <<traditional county>> at the northwestern extremity of north <<cc/Wales>>}}. It is separated from [[Caernarfonshire]] on the mainland by a narrow stretch of water called the [[Menai Strait]]. The county was merged into {{l|en|Gwynedd}} in 1974.
# {{place|en|A <<unitary authority>> in <<cc/Wales>>}}, {{w|Isle of Anglesey County Council}}, created in 1996 when it was separated from Gwynedd.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Miles Brignall|title=Victory against Vodafone for schoolteacher billed £15,000|magazine=w:The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/money/2014/nov/22/vodafone-pickpocket-bill-stolen-barcelona|date=2014-11-22|passage=Owain Roberts, from '''Anglesey''', was sent a bill for £4,300 by Vodafone.}}
# A [[marquisate]] in the [[peerage]] of the [[United Kingdom]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|Ynys Môn}}

