Page 31 it's all Greek to me: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{was wotd|2007|January|18}}
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Greek diphthongs.png|thumb|{{ux|en|This is definitely '''all Greek to me'''!}}]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|it's Greek to me|that's Greek to me|that's all Greek to me}}

===Etymology===
First quoted as “it was Greek to me” in ''{{w|Julius Caesar (play)|Julius Caesar}}'' by {{w|Shakespeare}}, maybe translated from a {{calque|en|ML.|-|notext=1}} sentence.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪts ˌɔːl ˈɡɹiːk tə ˌmiː/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-it's all Greek to me.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-it's all Greek to me.ogg|a=AU}}

===Phrase===
{{head|en|phrase}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} I don't [[understand]] any of it; it [[make sense|makes no sense]].
#: {{syn|en|it's all Chinese to me|[[make head or tail of|(I can’t) make head or tail of (it)]]|double Dutch}}
#: {{ux|en|I tried reading the instructions, but '''it’s all Greek to me'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Julius Caesar|act=I|scene=ii|page=112|column=1|passage=But thoſe that vnderſtood him, ſmil'd at one another, and ſhooke their heads: but for mine owne part, '''it was Greeke to me'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Rabelais Gargantua|volume=II|book=5|passage=During the processions they trilled and quavered most melodiously betwixt their teeth I do not know what antiphones, or chantings, by turns. For my part, '''’twas all Hebrew-Greek to me''', the devil a word I could pick out on’t; |brackets=on}}
#* {{RQ:Marryat Settlers|volume=II|chapter=XI|pages=181–182|pageref=182|passage="Well," said Alfred, "it may be a letter, but I confess '''it is all Greek to me'''. I certainly do not see why you wish to keep it a secret. Tell me."}}
#* {{RQ:Melville Redburn|chapter=He is Initiated in the Business of Cleaning Out the Pig-pen, and Slushing Down the Top-mast|page=45|passage=I ran after him, and received an order to go aloft and “slush down the main-top mast.” '''This was all Greek to me''', and after receiving the order, I stood staring about me, wondering what it was that was to be done.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1904
|author=[[w:George Manville Fenn|George M. Fenn]]
|title=The Ocean Cat's Paw
|passage=“Look here, Mr. Count,” he said; “I am only a rough Englishman, and a lot of what you have been saying about mission and that sort of thing is just so much '''Greek to me'''.”
}}
#* {{RQ:Wells War in the Air|passage=“It's more like some firm's paper. All this printed stuff at the top. Drachenflieger. Drachenballons. Ballonstoffe. Kugelballons. '''Greek to me'''.”}}
#* {{RQ:Gandhi Experiments|volume=II|chapter=VIII|passage=A Parsi lawyer was examining a witness and asking him question regarding credit and debit entries in account books. '''It was all Greek to me'''.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1965
|author=Harry Ray Bannister
|title=The Education of a Broadcaster
|page=16
|passage=Cavanaugh explained the network-affiliate relationship, which of course '''was all Greek to me''' and remained so even after his explanation.
}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=2004
|author=Jacob Taubes
|title=The Political Theology of Paul
|page=99
|passage={{...}}it was expected of me, or it was considered an honor, to lecture on seventeenth-century philosophy: Descartes (which '''was all Greek to me'''), Descartes to Spinoza.
}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|I don’t understand any of it}}
* Arabic: {{t|ar|يَتَحَدَّثْ بِٱللُّغَة ٱلصِّينِيَّة|lit=speaking in Chinese}}
* Armenian: {{t|hy|դա ինձ համար չինարեն է|lit=it's Chinese to me}}, {{t|hy|դրանից բան չեմ հասկանում|lit=I don't understand any of this}}
* Chavacano: {{t|cbk|Aleman ese comigo|lit=it's German to me}}
* Chinese:
*: Mandarin: {{t+|cmn|一竅不通|tr=yīqiàobùtōng}}, {{t+|cmn|一無所知|tr=yīwúsuǒzhī}}, {{t|cmn|完全不懂|tr=wánquán bùdǒng|lit=not understand at all}}, {{t|cmn|看起来像天书|tr=Kànqǐlái xiàng tiān shū}}, {{t|cmn|这是鬼画符吗|tr=Zhè shì guǐhuàfú ma}}, {{t|cmn|听起来像鸟语|tr=Tīngqǐlái xiàng niǎoyǔ}}, {{t+|cmn|火星文|tr=Huǒxīng wén|lit=Martian language}}
* Czech: {{t|cs|to je pro mě španělská vesnice|lit=it's a Spanish village to me}}, {{t+|cs|španělská vesnice|lit=a Spanish village}}
* Danish: {{t|da|rent volapyk|lit=pure Volapük}}, {{t|da|det er græsk for mig|lit=it is Greek to me}}, {{t|da|en by i Rusland|lit=a town in Russia}}
* Dutch: {{t|nl|dat is Chinees voor mij|lit=this is Chinese to me}}, {{qualifier|colloquial}} {{t|nl|[[ik]] [[er geen bal van verstaan|versta er geen bal van]]|lit=I don't understand a ball from it}}
* Esperanto: {{t|eo|[[ĝi]] [[estas]] [[por]] [[mi]] [[volapukaĵo]]}}
