Page 37 Wiktionary talk:Icelandic entry guidelines: -------- begin text --------
== Opinions and future additions ==

@[[User:GrænnHundur|GrænnHundur]], @[[User:Jöttur|Jöttur]], @[[User:Mannrinn|Mannrinn]], @[[User:Helrasincke|Helrasincke]] and @[[User:Benwing2|Benwing2]].

I have updated the page, please fix any errors you see and suggest anything that comes to mind for considerations we should take with Icelandic.

My additions are largely based off of @[[User:Vininn126|Vininn126's]] work on [[WT:About Polish]] but localized for Icelandic, of course. I updated information for each of the parts of speech. I did not provide intense detail for the noun declension template as that is available on the noun page. The verb and adverb templates are still untouched and so I have mentioned some shortcomings of the current templates. The adjective template is mostly complete but the documentation is not, so the text there can be changed later. Eventually, hopefully, a working pronunciation template will be available for us that we can mention here.
[[User:Anarhistička Maca|Anarhistička Maca]] ([[User talk:Anarhistička Maca|talk]]) 01:50, 14 February 2025 (UTC)

:Also @[[User:Caoimhin ceallach|Caoimhin ceallach]]. [[User:Anarhistička Maca|Anarhistička Maca]] ([[User talk:Anarhistička Maca|talk]]) 11:17, 14 February 2025 (UTC)
-------- end text --------
Page 38 Roman: -------- begin text --------
{{also|roman|román|Román|român|róman|Rómán}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fro|Romain}}, from {{der|en|la|Rōmānus}}. In reference to the Byzantine Empire, via the {{bor|en|gkm|-}} endonym {{m|grc|Ῥωμαῖος}}. {{surf|en|Rome|-an}}. {{doublet|en|Romano}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹəʊ.mən/|a=UK}}
* {{enPR|rōmən|a=US}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈɹoʊ.mən/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|Ro|man}}
* {{homophones|en|roamin'}} {{q|some accents}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊmən|s=2}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Roman.ogg|a=US}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of or from [[Rome]].
# {{lb|en|historical}} Of or from the Roman Empire. {{C|en|Ancient Rome}}
# {{lb|en|historical|historiography}} Of or from the [[Byzantine Empire]].
# Of [[noble]] [[countenance]] but with little facial [[expression]].
#* {{RQ:Landon Ethel Churchill|page=16|volume=III|passage="Yes, I feel that I ought; and with me, to feel that I ought to do a thing, is to do it!" added he, looking quite '''Roman''' with excess of virtue.}}
# {{lb|en|of type or text}} Supporting the [[character]]s of the [[Latin alphabet]].
# {{lb|en|law|colloquial}} {{non-gloss|Used to distinguish a [[Roman numeral]] from an [[Arabic numeral]] in oral discourse.}}
#: {{ux|en|You will find the term defined at the end of '''Roman''' one.}}
# {{lb|en|typography}} A font that is upright, as opposed to oblique or italic. (See [[roman font]].)
# Of or pertaining to the [[Roman Catholic]] Church or the [[Holy See]].
# {{lb|en|architecture}} Of a style characterised by the size and boldness of its round arches and vaults, and having baths, aqueducts, basilicas, amphitheatres, etc.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|Byzantine Roman}} {{l|en|Rhomaian}}, {{l|en|Romaic}}, {{l|en|Romaean}}

