===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A native or resident of [[Rome]].
# {{lb|en|historical}} A native or resident of the [[Roman Empire]].
# {{lb|en|historical|historiography}} A native or resident of the [[Byzantine Empire]].
#* '''2010''', John Wortley trans. John Skylitzes as ''A Synopsis of Byzantine History, 811{{ndash}}1057'', [https://books.google.com/books?id=vGE8Xq832A0C&pg=PA442 p. 442, n. 192]:
#*: [[Kars]] was the capital of the small Armenian kingdom of [[Vanand]], ruled by [[Gagik]] (the same name as the sovereign of [[Ani]]) from 1029 to 1064, when he surrendered his kingdom to the '''Romans'''. In 1053 it was taken by the [[Seljoukid]]s, probably under the command of Qutlumus...
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The Roman script.
# {{lb|en|printing|countable}} A single letter or character in Roman type.
# {{lb|en|dated}} A [[Roman Catholic]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=[[w:Sarah Waters|Sarah Waters]]|title=[[w:The Night Watch (Waters novel)|The Night Watch]]|publisher=Virago Press|page=151|passage=‘Is it like―I don’t know―Catholicism? One only spots the other '''Romans''' when one’s practised it oneself?’}}

