Page 39 mitosis: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|de|Mitose}}, from {{der|en|grc|μίτος||thread}} + {{af|en|-osis}}, probably in reference to the thread-like [[chromatin]] seen during mitosis.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/maɪˈtəʊ.sɪs/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mitosis.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/maɪˈtoʊ.sɪs/|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊsɪs|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|mitoses}}

# {{senseid|en|division of nucleus and often of cell, with euploid results}} {{lb|en|cytology}} The [[division]] of a cell [[nucleus]] in which the [[genome]] is copied and separated into two identical halves. It is normally followed by [[cell division]].
#: {{syn|en|q1=of nucleus|karyokinesis|karyomitosis}}
#: {{mer|en|prophase|metaphase|anaphase|telophase}}
#: {{cot|en|meiosis<id:type of cell division, in biology>}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|mitotic|pos=adj}}
* {{l|en|mitotically|pos=adv}}
* {{l|en|transmitosis}}

