* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈvɝd͡ʒ/|/daɪˈvɝd͡ʒ/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/dɑɪˈvɜːd͡ʒ/|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)dʒ|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|literally|of lines or paths}} To [[run]] [[apart]]; to [[separate]]; to [[tend]] into [[different]] [[direction]]s.
#* '''1916''', [[w:Robert Frost|Robert Frost]], “[[w:The Road Not Taken|The Road Not Taken]]” (poem), in ''[[w:Mountain Interval|Mountain Interval]]'':
#*: Two roads '''diverged''' in a yellow wood, / And sorry I could not travel both / {{...}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|figuratively|of interests, opinions, or anything else}} To become [[different]]; to run apart; to separate; to tend into different directions.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2012|author=Christoper Zara|title=Tortured Artists: From Picasso and Monroe to Warhol and Winehouse, the Twisted Secrets of the World's Most Creative Minds|section=part 1, chapter 1, {{gbooks|q=diverged|id=HV4jKhjzMVYC|pg=28}}
|passage=The brooding, black-clad singer bridged a stark divide that emerged in the recording industry in the 1950s, as post-Elvis pop singers '''diverged''' into two camps and audiences aligned themselves with either the sideburned rebels of rock 'n' roll or the cowboy-hatted twangsters of country music.}}
#: {{ux|en|Both stories start out the same way, but they '''diverge''' halfway through.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|literally|of a line or path}} To separate, to tend into a different direction (from another line or path).
#: {{ux|en|The sidewalk runs next to the street for a few miles, then '''diverges''' from it and turns north.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 October 20|author=Paul Stephen|title=Leisure and pleasure on the Far North Line|journal=RAIL|issue=942|page=49|text=North of Tain [...], the line reaches the southern shore of Dornoch Firth. Here, the railway and the A9 trunk road, which have hitherto run close together, '''diverge'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|figuratively|of an interest, opinion, or anything else}} To become [[different]], to separate (from another line or path).
#: {{ux|en|The software is pretty good, except for a few cases where its behavior '''diverges''' from user expectations.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|mathematics|of a sequence, series, or function}} Not to [[converge]]: to have no [[limit]], or no finite limit.
#: {{ux|en|2=The sequence <math>x_n = n^2</math> '''diverges''' to infinity: that is, it increases without bound.}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|converge}}

====Derived terms====
{{col|en|codiverge|divergement
|divergence}}
* {{l|en|divergent}}

