Page 59 agnostic: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{was wotd|2007|July|8}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵneh₃-}}
{{coin|en|Thomas Henry Huxley|in=1870}}. Either from {{der|en|grc|ἄγνωστος|t=ignorant, not knowing}}, or from {{af|en|a-<id:not>|Gnostic}}, deriving (either way) from {{der|en|grc|ἀ-|t=not}} + {{m|grc|γιγνώσκω|t=I know}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/aɡˈnɒstɪk/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/æɡˈnɑstɪk/|a=US,CA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-agnostic.ogg|a=US}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Simplificationalizer-agnostic.wav|a=New Jersey}}
* {{IPA|en|/æɡˈnɔstɪk/|a=AU}}
** {{audio|en|en-au-agnostic.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒstɪk|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[doubtful|Doubtful]] or [[uncertain]] about the existence or demonstrability of [[God]] or other [[deity]].
#: {{ux|en|She left the church when she had become '''agnostic'''.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|usually with a prepositional phrase}} Having no [[firm]]ly held [[opinion]]s on something.
#: {{ux|en|I'm '''agnostic''' on whether ethanol is a green fuel.}}
#: {{ux|en|He says he's '''agnostic''' concerning the Secretary's claims.}}
# Of or relating to [[agnosticism]] or its adherents.
#: {{ux|en|His '''agnostic''' viewpoint is summarized in his book.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1889
|title=Agnosticism
|author=w:Thomas Henry Huxley
|url=http://aleph0.clarku.edu/huxley/CE5/Agn.html
|passage=In matters of the intellect do not pretend that conclusions are certain which are not demonstrated or demonstrable. That I take to be the '''agnostic''' faith, which if a man keep whole and undefiled, he shall not be ashamed to look the universe in the face, whatever the future may have in store for him.
}}
# {{lb|en|computing|of a software component etc.}} [[unaware|Unaware]] or [[noncommittal]] regarding the specific nature of the [[component]]s or [[input]] with which it [[interact]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The socket communications layer is '''agnostic''' with regard to its underlying transport mechanism—it is “transport-'''agnostic'''”.}}
#: {{ux|en|The software's registration key is platform '''agnostic''' and will work on both x86 and ARM processors.}}

====Hyponyms====
* {{l|en|view agnostic}} {{qualifier|computing}}

====Derived terms====
{{col|en|agnostically|agnosticize|antiagnostic|nonagnostic|anti-agnostic|language-agnostic|location-agnostic|vendor agnostic|vendor-agnostic}}

====Related terms====
{{col3|en|agnosticism|apatheism|gnostic|ignostic|ignosticism}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|of or relating to agnosticism}}
* Arabic: {{t|ar|لَاأَدْرِيّ|m|tr=lā-ʔadriyy}}
* Asturian: {{t|ast|agnósticu}}
* Basque: {{t|eu|agnostiko}}
