Page 61 faðir: -------- begin text --------
{{also|faþir}}
==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fo|non|faðir}}, from {{inh|fo|gem-pro|*fadēr}}, from {{inh|fo|ine-pro|*ph₂tḗr}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|father}}, {{cog|de|Vater}}, {{cog|nds-de|Vader}}, {{m|nds-de|Voder}}, {{m|nds-de|Vadder}}, {{cog|is|faðir}}, {{cog|nb|far}}, {{m|nb|fader}}, {{cog|nn|far}}, {{m|nn|fader}}, {{cog|da|far}}, {{m|da|fader}}, {{cog|sv|far}}, {{m|sv|fader}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|fo|/ˈfɛaːjɪɹ/}}
* {{rhymes|fo|ɛaːjɪɹ}}

===Noun===
{{fo-noun|m|faðirs|fedrar|22=føður}}

# [[father]]

====Usage notes====
The oblique singular form {{l|fo|føður}} is very rare and limited to poetry.

====Declension====
{{fo-decl-noun-m43|faðir|fedr}}

===Anagrams===
* {{l|fo|farið}}, {{l|fo|friða}}

{{C|fo|Family}}

==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|faðir|t=father}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*fadēr}}, from {{inh|is|ine-pro|*ph₂tḗr}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|father}}, {{cog|de|Vater}}, {{cog|nds-de|Vader}}, {{m|nds-de|Voder}}, {{m|nds-de|Vadder}}, {{cog|fo|faðir}}, {{cog|nb|far}}, {{m|nb|fader}}, {{cog|nn|far}}, {{m|nn|fader}}, {{cog|da|far}}, {{m|da|fader}}, {{cog|sv|far}}, {{m|sv|fader}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈfaːðɪr/}}
* {{rhymes|is|aːðɪr}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# {{lb|is|higher register}} [[father]]
#: {{syn|is|pabbi<q:informal>|;|pápi<q:old-fashioned>|;|babbi<q:child's term, rare>}}
#* Judges 2:19
#*: {{quote|is|En er dómarinn andaðist, breyttu þeir að nýju verr en '''feður''' þeirra, með því að elta aðra guði til þess að þjóna þeim og falla fram fyrir þeim. Þeir létu eigi af gjörðum sínum né þrjóskubreytni sinni.|But when the judge died, the people returned to ways even more corrupt than those of their '''ancestors''', following other gods and serving and worshiping them. They refused to give up their evil practices and stubborn ways.}}
#: {{ux|is|Ég [[líta upp|lít upp]] til '''föður''' [[minn|míns]].|I look up to my '''father'''.}}
#: {{ux|is|Hvað heitir '''faðir''' þinn aftur?|What's your '''father's''' name again?}}

====Usage notes====
* The {{lg|nonstandard}} indefinite genitive singular '''föðurs(ins)''' is sometimes used but is {{lg|proscribed}}.
* For the proscribed feminine inflection, compare regional {{m|is|fjörður}}, also {{m|is|vetur}}, {{m|is|fingur}}, {{m|is|fótur}}, {{m|is|bróðir}} and to a lesser extent to nouns ending in {{m|is|-andi}} or {{m|is|-jandi}}.

====Declension====
