Page 79 Bavaria: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Bavária}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|Bavary||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|NL.|Bavaria}}, from {{der|en|ML.|Baioarii||Bavarians}}, from {{der|en|la|Boiuvarii|lit=[[Boii]] settlers}}, a compound of a {{der|en|cel-gau|-}} word meaning “cattle owner” (from {{der|en|cel-pro|*bāus||cow}}) + {{der|en|gem-pro|*warjaz||settler}}. Alternatively, {{w|Julius Pokorny|Pokorny}} proposes that the first element is a word meaning “warrior”, derived from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰeyh₂-||to hit, beat|id=strike}}. This name was adopted by the [[Marcomanni]] after defeating the Boii and settling [[Bohemia]] and parts of Bavaria.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bəˈvɛəɹiːə/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-Bavaria.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛəɹiə|s=4}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{place|en|historic region|r/Central Europe}}.
# The [[kingdom]] of Bavaria.
# One of the component states of [[Germany]] according to the current administrative division of the [[nation]], which includes the historical Bavaria and parts of [[Swabia]] and [[Franconia]].

