From {{inh|yi|gmh|Diutschlant}}, compound word formed from phrasings like {{m|gmh|[[diutsch]] [[lant]]|g=n}}, {{m|gmh|[[diutsch]]e [[lant]]|g=n}}, {{m|gmh|[[in]] [[diutsch]]eme [[lant|lande]]|g=n}}, {{m|gmh|[[ze]] [[diutisch]]eme [[lant|lande]]|g=n}}, {{m|gmh|([[in]]) [[diutsch]]iu [[lant]]|g=n-p}}. The adjective {{m|yi|דײַטש}} is from {{m+|gmh|diutsc}}, {{m|gmh|diutisch}}, {{m|gmh|diutsch}}, {{m|gmh|tiutsch}}, {{m|gmh|tiusch}}, from {{der|yi|goh|diutisc|t=of the people}}). Essentially {{af|yi|דײַטש|לאַנד|t1=German|t2=country}}.

