==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non}} ''*þes-'', ''þessi'' {{qualifier|neuter plural}}, {{m|non|sjá}} {{qualifier|nominative}},<ref name=gb>[http://books.google.se/books?id=vyOSYHXObjoC&pg=PA76&lpg=PA76&dq=sj%C3%A1+Old+Norse+etymology+demonstrative&source=bl&ots=3AqydwiXKT&sig=aHhOL9mT3LAREj0-EzH6_oDGBuc&hl=sv&ei=BI-ETryXJ8je4QT0grSGDw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=6&ved=0CE4Q6AEwBQ#v=onepage&q&f=false Old English and its relatives, Google books]</ref> related to and from the same ultimate origin as the irregular inflection of Old Norse {{m|non|sá}}, a descendant from the likewise irregularly inflected {{der|is|gem-pro|*sa}}.<ref name=gb/> Cognate with {{cog|ang|þes}} and {{cog|goh|dese}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈθɛsːɪ/}}
* {{rhymes|is|ɛsːɪ|s=2}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|pronoun|feminine|þessi|neuter|þetta}}

# {{lb|is|demonstrative}} [[this]], [[that]] (referring to both persons and things)

====Declension====
{{is-decl-pron-þessi}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|þetta er hebreska fyrir mér}}

===References===
<references />

{{cln|is|demonstrative pronouns}}

==Old Norse==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|non|sjá}}

===Etymology===
From the same ultimate origin as {{m|non|sá}} and {{m|non|þat}}. Related to {{cog|ang|se}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|þes}}, {{cog|goh|dese}}, {{cog|en|this}} and {{cog|de|diese}}.

===Pronoun===
{{head|non|pronoun|cat2=demonstrative pronouns|neuter|þetta}}

# {{alternative form of|non|sjá}}.

====Declension====
{{non-decl-pron-sjá}}
