Page 103 segja: -------- begin text --------
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
{{root|is|ine-pro|*sekʷ-|id=say}}
From {{inh|is|non|segja}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*sagjaną}}, ultimately from {{der|is|ine-pro|*sekʷ-||to say|id=say}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈseiːja/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|eiːja|s=2}}
*: {{homophones|is|seigja}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|sagði|sagt}}

# to [[say]], to [[tell]] {{+obj|is|dat}}
#* Isaiah 40 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Jesaja+40&version=ICELAND Icelandic], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Jesaja%2040&version=NIV English])
#*: {{quote|is|Heyr, einhver '''segir''': "Kalla þú!" Og ég svara: "Hvað skal ég kalla?" "Allt hold er gras og allur yndisleikur þess sem blóm vallarins. Grasið visnar, blómin fölna, þegar Drottinn andar á þau. Sannlega, mennirnir eru gras. Grasið visnar, blómin fölna, en orð Guðs vors stendur stöðugt eilíflega."|A voice '''says''', "Cry out." And I said, "What shall I cry?" "All men are like grass, and all their glory is like the flowers of the field. The grass withers and the flowers fall, because the breath of the LORD blows on them. Surely the people are grass. The grass withers and the flowers fall, but the word of our God stands forever."}}
#: {{ux|is|Ég '''segi''' söguna [[á eftir]].|I'll '''tell''' the story [[later]].}}
#: {{ux|is|'''Segðu''' mér eitthvað skemmtilegt.|'''Tell''' me something interesting.}}

====Usage notes====
This verb is cognate with English ''say'', but is sometimes used in places where ''tell'' or ''speak'' would be used in English, such as:
* {{uxi|is|'''segja''' [[brandari|brandara]]|to '''tell''' a joke}}

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj (segja)}}

====Derived terms====
{{col3|is
|hvað segir þú
|segja frá
|segja fyrir
|segjast
|segja til
|segja til syndanna
|segja upp
|{{l|is|segja þetta gott||call it a day}}
}}

[[Category:Most used Icelandic verbs]]

==Norwegian Nynorsk==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|nn|[[sigja]], [[sea]]||dialectal}}

===Etymology===
{{root|nn|ine-pro|*sekʷ-|id=say}}
From {{der|nn|non|segja}}, from {{der|nn|gem-pro|*sagjaną}}, ultimately from {{der|nn|ine-pro|*sekʷ-||to say|id=say}}. Akin to {{cog|en|say}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nn|/²sɛɪɑ/|/²sɛːjɑ/}} {{nn-pronu-note}}
* {{rhymes|nn|ɛɪɑ|ɛːjɑ}}
* {{hyphenation|nn|seg|ja}}

===Verb===
{{head|nn|verb|present tense|segjer|past tense|sa|or|sagde|supine|sagt|past participle|sagd|present participle|segjande|imperative|seg|f7alt=sèg}}

# {{lb|nn|[[Wiktionary:Norwegian_Nynorsk_spelling_reforms#1938|pre-1938]]}} to [[say]], [[tell]]; {{alt form|nn|nocap=1|seia}}
#: {{usex|nn|Kva skal du '''segja''' deim?|What are you going to '''tell''' them?}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|nn|segjand}}
* {{l|nn|segjande}}
* {{l|nn|segjande-sogn}}
* {{l|nn|segjing}}

===References===
* {{R:Aasen}}

{{catlangname|nn|pre-1938 forms}}

==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
{{root|non|ine-pro|*sekʷ-|id=say}}
