Page 123 Reconstruction:Proto-Slavic/grьkъ: -------- begin text --------
{{reconstructed}}
==Proto-Slavic==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|sla-pro|*grьčinъ}} (+ {{l|sla-pro|*-inъ}})

===Etymology===
Borrowed from Balkan {{bor|sla-pro|VL.|graecus}}, from {{der|sla-pro|grc|Γραικός}}, of uncertain origin.

It's not entirely clear why near-open -ae- was substituted with close *ь (*ĭ). On the one hand Simeonov proposed Thracian-related influence. On the other hand Skok and Shevelyov proposed that {{cog|VL.|grecíscus}} was borrowed into {{l|sla-pro|*grьčьskъ}} first, with back-formation of {{l|sla-pro|*grьci}} and {{l|sla-pro|*grьčinъ}}, and only then *grьkъ.

===Noun===
{{sla-noun|m|head=*grьkъ}}<ref>{{R:sla:SP|grьkъ|264|8}}</ref>

