==Proto-Germanic==

===Etymology===
{{unc|gem-pro}}. Often linked to {{m|gem-pro|*bōkō|t=beech}},<ref>{{R:gem:EDPG|page=71|head=*bōk-}}</ref> though beechbark-writing, unlike {{w|Birch bark manuscript|birchbark-writing}}, is not known, nor is it well imaginable that it was the time for [[bookfell]]s made from beeches already. Connected by some to {{der|gem-pro|ine-pro|*bʰeh₂g-|t=to allot}}, ascribing to the word the meaning of “letter”, in the sense of merely one or few symbols; {{rfv-etym|gem-pro}} in older times, letters would have served as (allotted) ownership symbols, which would then have been generalized to any work with writing upon it.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gem-pro|/bɔːks/}}

===Noun===
{{gem-noun|f}}

# [[letter]], written message, inscriptions carved into a flat object pressed together, “[[book]]”

====Inflection====
{{gem-decl-noun}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|gem-pro|*bōkastabaz}}
* {{l|gem-pro|*bōkalistiz}}
* {{l|gem-pro|*bōkārijaz}}
* {{l|gem-pro|*bōkōną}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|gem-pro|*bōkō}}

====Descendants====
* {{desctree|gmw-pro|*bōk}}
* {{desctree|non|bók}}

