==Proto-Indo-European==

===Etymology===
{{root|ine-pro|ine-pro|*werh₁-}}
From {{m|ine-pro|*werh₁-|t=to speak, say}}, with the extension {{m|ine-pro||*-dʰh₁-o-}} (from {{m|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-|t=to put}}), which expresses the perfective aspect. <ref>{{R:EWddS|ed=22|hw=Wort}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{ine-noun|n|-}}

# {{topics|ine-pro|Semantics}} [[word]]

====Inflection====
{{ine-decl-noun-n|werdʰh₁o}}
* Based on the different gradations in descendants, this word likely exhibited ablaut between the stems {{m|ine-pro||*wérdʰh₁- ~ *wordʰh₁- ~ *wr̥dʰh₁-}}; however, it has been [[thematicized]] in all descendants and so the particular declension type may be unreconstructible.
* It is possible that {{m+|la|verbum}} actually reflects the zero-grade or ''o''-grade, if it underwent an early shift {{m|la||*vor-}} > {{m|la||ver-}},<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=verbum|pages=664–665}}</ref> in which case the ''e''-grade would be unrepresented (unless {{m+|xum|𐌖𐌄𐌓𐌚𐌀𐌋𐌄||temple}} is a valid descendant).

====Descendants====
* {{desc|ine-bsl-pro|*wardas}} (from the [[o-grade]] {{m|ine-pro||*wordʰh₁om}})
** {{desc|ltg|vuords|t=word, name}}
** {{desc|lv|vārds|t=name, word}}
** {{desc|lt|var̃das|t=name}}
* {{desc|ine-bsl-pro|*wirdas}} (from the [[zero-grade]] {{m|ine-pro||*wr̥dʰh₁om}})
** {{desc|prg|wirds}}
** {{desc|urj-fin-pro|*virci|bor=1}} {{see desc}}
* {{desc|gem-pro|*wurdą}} (from the [[zero-grade]] {{m|ine-pro||*wr̥dʰh₁om}}<ref>[http://www.woerterbuchnetz.de/DWB?bookref=30,1467,2 “Wort” in: Deutsches Wörterbuch (Grimm)]</ref>) {{see desc}}
* {{desc|itc-pro|*werβom}} {{see desc}}

===References===
<references/>

===Further reading===
* {{R:ine:Hackstein:2002|14|section=3.2}}
