From {{inh|nn|non|mann}}, [[accusative|accusative case]] of {{m|non|maðr||man}} (compare the accusative of the {{cog|is|maður}}). Originally the word only had the sense "human" but later changed to primarily designate an adult male, the original meaning being replaced by words such as {{m|nn|menneske}} and {{m|nn|person}}. Believed to ultimately be from {{der|nn|gem-pro|*mann-}}, stemming from the {{der|nn|ine-pro|*man-|pos=a root}}. Cognate with {{cog|sv|man}}, {{cog|da|mand}}, {{cog|fo|-}} and {{cog|is|maður}}, {{cog|en|man}} and many others.

