==Rhymes==

===Two syllables===

{{col4|is
|'''áði'''<t:to stop to rest ''or'' eat ''while travelling''>
|'''bráði'''<t:to sparkle”; “a victim”, “an animal of prey”; “the near future”; “something which is melted”; “an eye’s expression”; “sudden”; “great”; “easily-angered>
|'''dáði'''<t:to admire ''something''”; “unconsciousness”; “admirably working>
|'''fáði'''<t:to take ''something''”, “to acquire ''something''”; “to give ''someone something''”; “with permission>
|'''fjáði'''<t:wealthy>
|'''fláði'''<t:to skin ''an animal''”; “a slope ''often of a cliffside''”; “overly friendly>
|'''gáði'''<t:to check”, “to observe”; “to take care of oneself”; “barking”; “sober>
|'''gljáði'''<t:to shine”; “a frozen wetland (''dated'')”, “an {{l|en|ice floe}} (''dated'')”; “shining>
|'''gráð'''<t:a measurement of sea level”; “a slight snowfall”; “crates by an alter”; “sexually stimulated”; “not barking>
|'''háði'''<t:to participate ''in a battle or competition''”; “to work in {{l|en|haymaking}}”; “an argument in written ''or'' spoken form meant to mock and deride ''someone''”; “controlled ''by someone or circumstances''>
|'''hrjáði'''<t:to torment ''someone''”; “extremely stressed>
|'''hváði'''<t:to ask someone to repeat what they said>
|'''kljáði'''<t:to resolve ''a problem''>
|'''láði'''<t:to blame ''or'' accuse (''used in negative or question clauses'')”; “to lure ''someone else to oneself''”; “a country (''poetic'')>
|'''ljáði'''<t:to lend ''someone something''”; “to mention ''something'' (''governs the genative case'')>
|'''máði'''<t:to deface ''often through blurring''”; “faded>
|'''náði'''<t:to succeed in attaining or getting ahold of something”; “to have time for ''something''”; “to span ''a distance, time, or amount''”; “to get ''somewhere''”; “to pass ''an exam''”; “to hear, understand, ''or'' commit something to memory”; “to recover”; “to reduce the sentence of a crime>
|'''ráði'''<t:to negotiate the beginning of someone's employment”; “to deduce”; “to have fury”; “to control (''governs the dative case'')”; “to advise (''governs the dative case'')”;  “counsel”, “a council”; “a plan>
|'''sáði'''<t:to sow”; “a seed”; “semen”; “(an) {{l|en|inoculum}}”; “poorly-ground ''or'' unground grain (''dated'')>
|'''skráði'''<t:to list ''something or'' put ''something'' on a list“; ”to write ''something or'' put ''something'' into print”; “a list“; “a unit of computer data”; “a door's lock”; “listed>
|'''snáði'''<t:a little boy>
|'''snjáði'''<t:to become worn out”; “worn>
|'''spáði'''<t:to predict“; ”to guess”; “a tool or utensil with a handle ''i.e. a spatula or tennis racket''”; “a playing card suit”; “a propeller ''or'' fan blade>
|'''stráði'''<t:to spread ''a fine substance''“; ”a blade of grass“; ”an old, unhealthy person>
|'''tjáði'''<t:to express ''an opinion''“; ”to tell ''someone something''“; ”a mess>
|'''þáði'''<t:to accept ''or'' recieve>
|'''þjáði'''<t:to cause ''someone'' agony“; ”tormented>
|'''þráði'''<t:to long ''for someone or somewhere''“; ”a strong desire“; ”a thread“, ”a plot thread“, ”a thread of discussion (''in an online chatroom'')>
}}
