====Conjugation====
{{fo-conj-ráða}}

==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|ráða}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*rēdaną}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*Hreh₁dʰ-||reason, count}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|read}}, {{cog|nds|raden}}, {{cog|nl|raden}}, {{cog|de|raten}}, {{cog|sv|råda}}, {{cog|got|𐌲𐌰𐍂𐌴𐌳𐌰𐌽}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|grc|ἀριθμός}}, {{cog|sga|immrádim}}, {{cog|cu|радити}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈrauːða/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|auːða|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|réð|réðu|ráðið}}

# {{lb|is|with accusative}} to [[employ]], to [[hire]]
#: {{ux|is|Hún '''ræður''' alltaf vini sína.|She always '''employs''' her friends.}}
#: {{ux|is|Ég mætti bara [[brosa]]ndi og ég var '''ráðinn''' [[á staðnum]].|I just showed up [[smile|smiling]] and I was '''hired''' [[on the spot]].}}
# {{lb|is|with accusative}} to [[solve]]
#: {{ux|is|Geturðu '''ráðið''' þessar gátur?|Can you '''solve''' these riddles?}}
# {{lb|is|with accusative}} to [[read]]
#: {{ux|is|Hann '''réð''' rúnirnar.|He '''read''' the runes}}
# {{lb|is|with dative}} to [[command]], [[control]], be in control of
#: {{ux|is|Hver '''ræður''' hér í raun og veru?|Who is really in charge here?}}
# {{lb|is|ditransitive|with dative and accusative}} to [[advise]] (someone to do something)
#: {{ux|is|Afi minn '''réð''' mér alltaf heilt.|My grandfather always gave me good advice.}}
# {{lb|is|with dative}} to [[decide]]
#: {{ux|is|Ég læt þig '''ráða'''.|I'll let you '''decide'''.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|ráðast}}
* {{l|is|það verður að ráðast}} (it will have to take its course)

[[Category:Most used Icelandic verbs]]

==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
{{root|non|ine-pro|*Hreh₁dʰ-}}
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*rēdaną}}, from {{inh|non|ine-pro|*Hreh₁dʰ-}}.

===Verb===
{{non-verb|réð|réðu|ráðinn}}

# {{lb|non|ditransitive|with dative and accusative}} to {{l|en|advise}}, {{l|en|counsel}} (someone to do something)
# {{lb|non|transitive|with dative}} to {{l|en|consult}} about, {{l|en|discuss}}
# {{lb|non|with dative}} to {{l|en|devise}}, {{l|en|plan}}
# {{lb|non|with dative}} to {{l|en|agree}} on
#: {{ux|non|réðu þeir þat þá með sér|they settled this among themselves}}
# {{lb|non|with accusative}} to {{l|en|fix}}, {{l|en|resolve}}
#: {{ux|non|hefi áðr ráðit brúðlaup mitt|I have fixed my wedding day}}
# {{lb|non|with accusative}} to {{l|en|hire}}, take into service
#: {{ux|non|bóndi sagði húsfreyju, at hann hafði Hrapp ráðit með sér|the partisan told his wife that he had taken Hrapp into his company}}
# {{lb|non|with dative}} to {{l|en|rule}} (over), {{l|en|govern}}
#: {{ux|non|Einarr jarl réð þá Orkneyjum|Earl Einarr ruled the Orkneys}}
# {{lb|non|with dative}} to {{l|en|rule}}, {{l|en|command}}, have one's way with, {{l|en|prevail}}, {{l|en|decide}}, {{l|en|settle}}
# {{lb|non|with dative}} to {{l|en|have}}, {{l|en|possess}}, be master of, {{l|en|enjoy}}
# {{lb|non|with dative}} to {{l|en|explain}}, {{l|en|read}}, {{l|en|interpret}}
# {{lb|non|with accusative}} to {{l|en|read}} and {{l|en|understand}} (e.g. [[rune]]s)

====Conjugation====
{{non-conj-strong|class=7|ráð|1i=ræð|1is=ræz|1s=ráz|réð|2t=rét|2s=réz|réð|ráð}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|non|ᚱᛅᚦᛅ||infinitive|Runic form}}
* {{alter|non|ᚱᛅᚦᚱ||second/third singular present indicative|Runic form}}
* {{alter|non|ᚱᛁᚦ|ᚱᛆᛁᚦ||first/third singular past indicative|Runic form}}
* {{alter|non|ᚱᛅᚦᛁ|ᚱᚮᚦᛁ||third singular present subjunctive|Runic form}}
* {{alter|non|ᚱᛅᚦ||second singular imperative|Runic form}}

