===Etymology===
{{inh+|is|non|maðr}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*mann-}}, probably ultimately from {{der|is|ine-pro|*mánu-||person}}, {{m|ine-pro|*man-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈmaðʏr/|[ˈmäːð̠˕ʏr̥]}}
*: {{audio|is|Is-maður.ogg|a=Iceland,Kópavogur}}
*: {{rhymes|is|aːðʏr|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|manns|menn}}

# [[human being]], [[person]], [[humanity]], [[mankind]], [[man]] (generic)
#: {{ux|is|Það tilheyrir náttúru '''mannsins''' að hata þá sem hann hefur sært.|It belongs to '''human''' nature to hate those that he has hurt.}}
#* Timothy 2:11-12 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1+Timothy+2:11-12&version=NIV English], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1%20Timothy%202:11-12&version=ICELAND Icelandic])
# [[man]], [[adult]] [[male]] individual
#: {{ux|is|Ég sá '''mann''' úti á götu.|I saw a '''man''' out on the street}}
#: {{ux|is|Þá sendi Benhadad menn til að njósna. Þeir sögðu honum svo frá: "'''Menn''' fara út frá Samaríu."|and Ben-hadad sent out, and they told him, saying, There are '''men''' come out of Samaria. 1 Kings 20:17}}

# {{lb|is|mainly used with a definite article}} [[husband]]
#: {{ux|is|Þetta er Geir, '''maðurinn''' minn.|This is Geir, my '''husband'''.}}
# {{lb|is|chess}} chess [[piece]], [[chessman]]
#: {{ux|is|Færðu '''manninn''' þinn.|Move your '''piece'''.}}

