===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|non|kvenna|kvinna}}
* {{alter|non|kuna}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*kwenǭ}}, ultimately from {{inh|non|ine-pro|*gʷḗn||woman}}.

===Noun===
{{non-noun|f|konu|konur}}

# [[woman]]
# [[wife]]

====Declension====
{{non-decl-f-on|kon|gp=kvenna|notes=Note the form '''{{l|non|kvenna}}''' in genitive plural.}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|non|karl|g=m}}

====Derived terms====
Many of the derivatives use the genitive plural {{m|non|kvenna|kvenna-}}, or the shorter {{m|non|kvenn-}}, which effectively forms an independent prefix pertaining to women or to womanhood. This is also the origin of the alternative form {{m|non|kvinna|g=f}}, whence also some of its modern Scandinavian descendants.
{{prefixsee|non|kvenn-}}
{{der4|non|{{l|non|áburðarkona|g=f||a showy, dressy woman}}
