Page 285 kamikaze: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|ja|-}} {{ja-r|神風|かみ​かぜ|gloss=divine wind}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌkæ.mɪˈkɑː.zi/|a=RP}}
* {{qualifier|emulating Japanese}} {{IPA|en|/kɑː.mɪˈkɑː.zeɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-kamikaze.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[attack]] requiring the [[suicide]] of the one carrying it out, especially when done with an [[aircraft]].
# One who carries out a [[suicide attack]], especially with an aircraft.
# A [[vehicle]] used for a suicide attack, especially an aircraft.
#* {{quote-av|en|author=Drachinifel|title=The Mark 14 Torpedo - Failure is Like Onions|date=12 February 2020|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eQ5Ru7Zu_1I|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221124003326/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eQ5Ru7Zu_1I|archivedate=24 November 2022|accessdate=26 November 2022|time=8:16|text=Coupled with this were issues involving ''actually getting enough torpedoes out there to the fleet in the first place!''  Whilst they ''were'' a munition, a torpedo is ''far'' more complex and took far longer to build than a shell for a naval gun, even a battleship shell.  Torpedoes, remember, are effectively small self-guiding '''kamikaze''' submarines, and, so, unless you have a large factory and an extensive production line going, you're only gonna see ''handfuls'' produced each year.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} One who takes excessive risks, as for example in a sporting event.
# A [[cocktail]] made of equal parts [[vodka]], [[triple sec]] and [[lime juice]].
# {{lb|en|surfing}} A [[deliberate]] [[wipeout]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|kamikaze drone}}

