{{trans-bottom}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[suicidal|Suicidal]], [[risk]]ing one's own [[life]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=w:Robert Draper|title=They are Watching You—and Everything Else on the Planet: Technology and Our Increasing Demand for Security have Put Us All under Surveillance. Is Privacy Becoming just a Memory?|url=https://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/2018/02/surveillance-watching-you/|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20180614211931/https://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/2018/02/surveillance-watching-you/|archivedate=14 June 2018|magazine=w:National Geographic|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=w:National Geographic Society|month=February|year=2018|issn=0027-9358|oclc=1049714034|passage=Sheathed in helmets, gloves, and jackets, they look more like manic video game figures than humans. They weave through traffic and around double-decker buses at '''kamikaze''' velocity.}}
# Having or showing reckless disregard for safety or personal welfare.

