===Etymology===
From {{der|ceb|en|under}}, from {{der|ceb|ang|under}}, from {{der|ceb|gem-pro|*under}} (whence also {{cog|de|unter}}, {{cog|nl|onder}}, Danish and {{cog|no|under}}), from a merger of {{der|ceb|ine-pro|*n̥dʰér|t=under}} and {{m|ine-pro|*n̥tér||inside}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|ceb|an|der}}

===Adjective===
{{head|ceb|adjective}}

# [[henpecked]]
# [[uxorious]]
# [[submissive]]

===Verb===
{{head|ceb|verb}}

# to [[domineer]]
# to [[intimidate]]

{{categorize|ceb|Cebuano idioms}}

==Central Franconian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|gmw-cfr|anger||Ripuarian, now chiefly western dialects}}
* {{alter|gmw-cfr|anner||chiefly Moselle Franconian}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|gmw-cfr|gmh|ander}}, from {{inh|gmw-cfr|goh|andar}}.

The form is non-native in Central Franconian and borrowed from standard {{der|gmw-cfr|de|anderer}} in those eastern and central Ripuarian dialects that often replace their inherited ''-ng-'' with ''-nd-''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gmw-cfr|/ˈandʌ/}}

===Adjective===
{{head|gmw-cfr|adjective|masculine|andere|feminine|ander}}

# {{lb|gmw-cfr|some dialects of|_|Ripuarian}} [[other]]
# {{lb|gmw-cfr|some dialects of|_|Ripuarian}} [[different]]

==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|ander}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|andar}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*anþar}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*anþeraz}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ˈɑn.dər/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-ander.ogg|audio}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|an|der}}
* {{rhyme|nl|ɑndər|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{nl-adj|-}}

# {{l|en|other}}
#:{{ux|nl|Kun je me een '''ander''' boek aanraden?|Can you recommend me another book?}}
#:{{ux|nl|De kat speelde met het ene speeltje en negeerde het '''andere''' speeltje.|The cat played with one toy and ignored the '''other''' toy.}}
#:{{ux|nl|Er zijn veel manieren om dit probleem op een '''andere''' manier op te lossen.|There are many ways to solve this problem in a '''different''' manner.}}
# {{l|en|different}}
#:{{ux|nl|Ze koos een '''ander''' restaurant voor het diner.|She chose a '''different''' restaurant for dinner.}}
#:{{ux|nl|De twee schilderijen zijn van dezelfde kunstenaar, maar ze hebben een '''andere''' stijl.|The two paintings are by the same artist, but they have a '''different''' style.}}
#:{{ux|nl|Het nieuwe ontwerp ziet er '''anders''' uit dan het vorige.|The new design looks '''different''' from the previous one.}}
# {{lb|nl|archaic}} {{l|en|second}}

====Inflection====
Note: The predicative/adverbial form is {{m|nl|anders}}, identical to the partitive form.
{{nl-decl-adj||-|pred=anders}}

====Derived terms====
